<article class="env-lemma" id="0BZD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BZD">Lemma <span data-tag="0BZD">47.13.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0BZB" data-tag="0BZB">47.13.6</a> assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$E$ viewed as an object of $D(R)$ is compact, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$N = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits ^\bullet _ R(E^\bullet , R)$ computes $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E, R)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E, -) : D(R) \to D(E)$ is isomorphic to $K \mapsto K \otimes _ R^\mathbf {L} N$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Special case of Differential Graded Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BZ0" data-tag="0BZ0">22.33.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>